window.products.push({"id":82599,"name":"Easy to Install RCO410 3-in-1 Hard Start Kit for Refrigerators RC0410 Supco ERP410 RCO410 3 in 1 Compressor Hard Start Capacitor - Replaces TJ90RCO410","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71FE4t26a0L._SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Rco410 Start Kit - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers TJ90RCO410, AP4503017, 600-410, ERP410, HS410, RC0410, RCO-410. Fits different compressor types including RSIR, CSIR, PSC, and CSR compressors. Supco Rco410 Start Kit outperforms all competitors. One of the benefits of using the Rco410 Relay is that it can help extend the life of a refrigerator compressor, which is one of the most expensive components in a refrigerator. This kit is #1 choice for a refrigerator compressor. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Rco410 Start Kit assists your refrigerator or freezer compressor with enduring longer. It allows the compressor to bring down your power bill. The Rco410 Start Relay Combo Kit is easy to install and can be used with a variety of refrigerator brands and models. 💡 The 3n1 Start Rco410 Kit is designed to help a refrigerator's compressor start more efficiently and reduce the chances of compressor failure. The Rco410 Hard Start Kit is used to replace existing start relays, capacitors, and overloads in refrigeration systems that use 1/4 to 1/3 horsepower compressors. Refrigerator Rco410 3 1 Start Relay Kit meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do you test a 3 in 1 start relay? To test a 3in1 start relay, follow these steps: Turn off power to the appliance. Check the continuity of the overload protector and start capacitor. Check the resistance of the start and run windings. Test the relay operation by connecting it to the compressor and turning on the power. If the relay is working correctly, the compressor should start to run. If any of these tests fail, the relay may be faulty and need replacement. 💡 How do I check if a relay is bad? To check if a refrigerator relay is bad, follow these steps: Listen for unusual noises, check the continuity of the overload protector and start capacitor, check the resistance of the start and run windings. It is also recommended to visually inspect the relay for any signs of physical damage or burning. If the relay is physically damaged or shows signs of burning, it needs to be replaced with a new RCO410 3-in-1 Hard Start Kit.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71FE4t26a0L._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07MLV25P9","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-82599","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MLV25P9","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07MLV25P9","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
